    "updated_at": "2022-02-28T07:59:29Z",
    "body": "There are multiple ways to achieve this for the time being.\r\nWith custom functions:\r\n```pwsh\r\n# shipadmin.ps1\r\n# put this file somewhere in your path\r\n\r\n#Requires -RunAsAdministrator\r\n```\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[custom.psadmin]\r\nformat = \"[Admin]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bold green\"\r\nos = \"windows\"\r\nwhen = 'powershell -NoProfile .\\shipadmin.ps1'\r\n```\r\nThis however is extremely slow.\r\n\r\nA much better alternative that uses environment variables.\r\n```pwsh\r\n# Microsoft.Powershell_profile.ps1\r\n\r\nif (([Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal] [Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent()).IsInRole([Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole] \"Administrator\")) {$Env:SHIPADMIN = $True}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[env_var.SHIPADMIN]\r\nvariable = \"SHIPADMIN\"\r\nformat = \"[Admin]($style)\"\r\nstyle = \"bold green\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/91775495/155945782-75156361-9199-4d0e-b835-55a72f528de0.png)\r\n",
